We added a script block with sections: CONFIG, STATE, etc. Now need to add a main loop implementation.

Specifically, need to add startLoop() function that includes cancelAnimationFrame handling, and a requestAnimationFrame loop wrapped in try/catch that calls update(dt) and render().

We need to place it in the appropriate // === SECTION === block. The existing script contains two sections: // === CONFIG ... and // === STATE. There is no // === LOOP / UPDATE or // === RENDER etc. According to reference template, we should create a // === LOOP/UPDATE section (named // === UPDATE? Actually reference uses // === UPDATE section for update function. For loop start, they probably have a function startLoop() and maybe it belongs after STATE section but before UPDATE? The reference example had:

- CONFIG
- STATE
- RESET
- LOOP/UPDATE (merged: startLoop, update)
- RENDER
- INPUT
- AUDIO
- OBSERVABLE CONTRACT
- BOOT.

But we have only defined STATE; not reset, not loop, no update/render yet. This is task 3: "Main loop implementation — add startLoop() with cancelAnimationFrame handling, a requestAnimationFrame loop wrapped in try/catch that calls update(dt) and render()."

Thus we should create a new section within the script: maybe // === LOOP =============================================================.

We need to add the function definitions startLoop, tick, update (placeholder?), render (placeholder?) maybe empty placeholder functions or just call them (they might not exist yet). The page must load without console errors. So we either need to define empty stub functions update and render (no errors). The spec: the startLoop calls update(dt) and render() each tick. If update and render do not exist at load, we need to add stub definitions.

Thus we need to edit the script block after the STATE definitions to add a new section // === LOOP ============================================================= that defines startLoop, tick (maybe inside startLoop), plus stub definitions for update and render (maybe separate sections later). But we need to consider later tasks: they will fill out update logic and render code. We need to supply placeholders that won't break later tasks (they will be overwritten later perhaps). So we can create empty functions update(dt){ } and render(){ } as placeholders.

Also we need startLoop function that cancels prior loop and sets requestAnimationFrame.

Add code:

function startLoop() {
    if (loopId !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(loopId);
    function tick(now) {
        try {
            const dt = Math.min((now - lastTime) / 1000, 0.1);
            lastTime = now;
            update(dt);
            render();
        } catch (err) {
            console.error("loop error", err);
        }
        loopId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    }
    loopId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
}

We also need to call startLoop somewhere perhaps after defining functions? Perhaps the boot later will call reset etc. Not required now. Page must load. So we don't need to start loop yet.

Place this after the existing state definitions (currently there are let player, hazards..., etc). Insert after those lines.

